{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791584463,"nonce":"z6ogLKHvPX/5zymdQtT98sF0zx0=","message":"The core button and cn::button are off Stateful (local: 61d8598a record, b01479e1, 20af29c6, 617b0722; signal-bound when() in 696122f2).\n\nAPI change, as agreed: button(label) and button_with(|look| content) replace button(state, label) and button_with(state, |state| content). No SharedState handle, no on_state, no deps, no config_arc. key() names the pointer state (needed for buttons made in a loop from one place), disabled takes a bool, a State or a Computed, and a click is ignored while disabled. A content builder is called once with a ButtonLook (text_color() computed, interaction()), so state-dependent content binds instead of being rebuilt. New options for a disabled look: disabled_text_color, disabled_border, flat_when_disabled. Div gained shadows(..) (whole stack, can follow a signal) and a border_width that can follow a signal.\n\ncn::button with a signal-bound disabled used to rebuild its subtree; it now restyles in place (fill, text, border, shadow). Checked by comparing a signal-disabled button with a button built disabled, both ways. The class cn-button--disabled is still added only when the button is built disabled.\n\nBehaviour change found by the recordings: the old button mutated its shared config, so a stylesheet :hover text colour stuck after the pointer left. The new one resolves each state separately. Recorded in the commit.\n\nRecordings (tests/{toggle,checkbox,radio,button}_states.rs and .golden in blinc_cn) now init a fixed theme (Hybrid, dark). They had followed the system theme, so CI failed on all three OSes on d1df29a0. The goldens were regenerated from the widgets as they were before each migration; toggle, checkbox and radio match them exactly, button differs only in the hover-colour lines above.\n\nStill stateful in cn: checkbox (own closure), and the rest of the 